    "https://marietta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204593": {
      "title": "Administrative Coordinator",
      "description": "Marietta College\nJob Posting: Administrative Coordinator - Physician Assistant Program Marietta College \n\tJob Posting: Administrative Coordinator - Physician Assistant Program Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Administrative Coordinator - Physician Assistant Program Category: Staff Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Physician Assistant Locations: Marietta, OH Posted: Sep 9, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Hourly Position ID: 204593 Share About Marietta College: For nearly two centuries, Marietta College has embraced its commitment to serving young adults seeking to better their lives and to turn their life's passions into actionable good in the world. Committed to a contemporary liberal arts education and home to the 16th oldest chapter of Phi Beta Kappa, Marietta offers more than 40 undergraduate programs as well as graduate programs in Physician Assistant Studies, Sustainability Leadership, and Psychology. At Marietta, students learn from talented faculty members who are respected in their fields and wholly dedicated to teaching the next generation of leaders. Our professors share their knowledge with students and challenge them to develop their skillsets through serious research, experiential opportunities, and internships. Every student completes Marietta's rigorous General Education Curriculum, which builds strong communication skills and exposes students to new ideas and interests. Our varsity athletic teams compete in NCAA Division III and against some of the best in the nation as a member of the Ohio Athletic Conference and Mid-Atlantic Rowing Conference. Marietta has won six national championships and 64 conference titles, including an OAC-record 46 baseball titles. More than 26,000 living members of The Long Blue Line proudly support their alma mater and help current students gain internships and connections into their chosen industries. This support, in addition to the vibrant growth on campus, is one of the reasons why The Chronicle of Higher Education named Marietta College one of the Great Colleges to Work For. The College sits on 90 picturesque acres in Marietta, Ohio, located just blocks from a historic downtown and the Ohio River. For more information about the College, please visit marietta.edu . Job Description: This position provides essential administrative support to faculty, staff, students, preceptors, and clinical sites. This role supports the smooth operation of the program by managing shared communications and email triage, coordinating routine clinical rotation correspondence, maintaining records, student files, and databases, tracking student compliance and onboarding requirements, scheduling, and general office processes. Essential Functions of the Position: Serve as the first point of contact and triage hub for students, faculty, preceptors, clinical sites, and external stakeholders, and route nonroutine questions to the appropriate faculty or staff member. Manage schedules, coordinate meetings, and organize events for the program. Maintain accurate records, student files, and databases. Assist with the preparation of accreditation and compliance reports. Manage program communications, including monitoring shared email accounts, responding to routine inquiries, and coordinating timely follow up in a professional manner. Support faculty with administrative tasks, including exam proctoring, course material distribution, and document preparation. Support the clinical team with administrative tasks, expense reports, preceptor payments, tuition credit, and portal management. Also coordinate routine clinical rotation correspondence, including confirmation letters, required forms, schedule notices, and communications to students, preceptors, and clinical sites under the direction of the Program Director and Clinical Coordinator. Assist with budget tracking, purchasing, and expense reports. Coordinate travel arrangements for faculty and staff as needed. Ensure office supplies are stocked and maintained. Track student compliance and onboarding requirements for the clinical year, including immunizations, background checks, and required site or hospital documentation, notifying the Program Director and Clinical Coordinator of missing or overdue items. Perform clinical support duties under the direction of the Program Director and Clinical Coordinator.  This includes obtaining approval for clinical sites, student placements, evaluating student performance, and academic progression decisions from the Program Director and Clinical Coordinator. Requirements: Required Skills and Abilities: Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to manage high volume email and telephone communication professionally. Strong organizational and multitasking abilities. Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information. Required Experience & Education: Associate or bachelor's degree in business administration, education, healthcare administration or related field preferred. Minimum of two years of administrative experience, preferably in a PA program, health professions program, higher education, or healthcare setting. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook). Experience managing shared inboxes, maintaining confidential student records, and tracking time sensitive compliance requirements is preferred. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references. All applications/resumes must be submitted through this online process. We regret that we are unable to accept applications or resumes submitted by mail, email, or fax. As you are submitting your application via this online process, please be sure to provide an accurate email address. You will then receive an acknowledgment indicating your application materials have been received. Marietta College is an equal opportunity educator and employer. Marietta College does not discriminate on the basis of age, race, color, gender orientation, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, religion, sex, pregnancy (including childbirth, lactation and related medical conditions), physical or mental disability, genetic information (including testing and characteristics), veteran status, uniformed service member status, political affiliation, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local laws. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Marietta College 215 Fifth Street, Marietta, OH 45750"
    },
    "https://marietta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205137": {
      "title": "Director of Entrepreneurship and Assistant Professor of Business",
      "description": "Marietta College\nJob Posting: Director of Entrepreneurship and Assistant Professor of Business Marietta College \n\tJob Posting: Director of Entrepreneurship and Assistant Professor of Business Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Director of Entrepreneurship and Assistant Professor of Business Category: Faculty Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Business & Economics Locations: Marietta, OH Posted: Sep 24, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Position ID: 205137 Share About Marietta College: For nearly two centuries, Marietta College has embraced its commitment to serving young adults seeking to better their lives and to turn their life's passions into actionable good in the world. Committed to a contemporary liberal arts education and home to the 16th oldest chapter of Phi Beta Kappa, Marietta offers more than 40 undergraduate programs as well as graduate programs in Physician Assistant Studies, Sustainability Leadership, and Psychology. At Marietta, students learn from talented faculty members who are respected in their fields and wholly dedicated to teaching the next generation of leaders. Our professors share their knowledge with students and challenge them to develop their skillsets through serious research, experiential opportunities, and internships. Every student completes Marietta's rigorous General Education Curriculum, which builds strong communication skills and exposes students to new ideas and interests. Our varsity athletic teams compete in NCAA Division III and against some of the best in the nation as a member of the Ohio Athletic Conference and Mid-Atlantic Rowing Conference. Marietta has won six national championships and 64 conference titles, including an OAC-record 46 baseball titles. More than 26,000 living members of The Long Blue Line proudly support their alma mater and help current students gain internships and connections into their chosen industries. This support, in addition to the vibrant growth on campus, is one of the reasons why The Chronicle of Higher Education named Marietta College one of the Great Colleges to Work For. The College sits on 90 picturesque acres in Marietta, Ohio, located just blocks from a historic downtown and the Ohio River. For more information about the College, please visit marietta.edu . Job Description: Marietta College invites applications for a tenure-track Director of Entrepreneurship and Assistant Professor of Business beginning August 2027. The successful candidate will join the Department of Business & Economics, one of the College's largest academic units, which offers eight majors: Accounting, Economics, Entrepreneurship, Finance, Land & Energy Management, Management, Marketing, and Sport Management. The successful candidate will provide leadership for the Entrepreneurship program while teaching courses that support the department's core curriculum. The position also offers the opportunity to teach in Marietta College's new MBA program. We seek a dynamic teacher-scholar with expertise in management, business ethics, human resource management, or related business fields. The successful candidate should be prepared to teach core business courses, contribute to student career development, engage with the regional business community, and support entrepreneurship programming across campus. In addition to teaching and scholarship, the candidate will provide leadership for key co-curricular entrepreneurship initiatives, including the PioBiz competition, the Big Blue thrift store, and the entrepreneurship mentor network. Because of these administrative and programmatic responsibilities, the position may include a reduced teaching load. Essential Functions Teach a load determined in consultation with Academic Affairs and the department chair, with consideration given to the administrative and programmatic responsibilities of the Director of Entrepreneurship role. Teach courses in entrepreneurship and core business areas such as management, business ethics, human resource management, global business, introductory management, and other courses aligned with departmental needs and candidate expertise. Serve as Director of the Entrepreneurship Program, providing leadership for entrepreneurship curriculum, student engagement, program development, and cross-campus collaboration. Coordinate and oversee major entrepreneurship co-curricular initiatives, including the PioBiz competition and the Big Blue thrift store. Recruit, develop, and coordinate community mentors and entrepreneurship partners to support student learning, venture development, and professional growth. Build relationships with regional entrepreneurs, business leaders, alumni, and organizations to expand experiential learning, internship, mentoring, and community-partnership opportunities. Support the continued growth, visibility, assessment, and recruitment of entrepreneurship programming across the College. Serve as an academic advisor, maintaining an active portfolio of advisees and meeting with students regularly for course registration and academic planning. Act as a positive mentor for Marietta College students, fostering intellectual growth, career readiness, entrepreneurial thinking, and professional development. Engage in scholarship and research, broadly defined to include applied, pedagogical, and disciplinary work. Participate in service to the College and department, including committee work, student recruitment, departmental meetings, and other duties appropriate to a tenure-track faculty appointment. Requirements: Required Qualifications An earned MBA or another relevant master's degree with substantial entrepreneurial, business leadership, professional, and/or college-level teaching experience. Demonstrated commitment to teaching excellence, student mentoring, and experiential learning in a contemporary liberal arts environment. Ability to teach one or more core business areas consistent with departmental needs. Additional Information: Preferred Qualifications An earned doctorate (PhD, DBA, or equivalent) in entrepreneurship, management, business administration, or a closely related field is preferred. Demonstrated experience in entrepreneurship education, venture development, innovation, startup activity, or small business leadership. Eperience coordinating programs, competitions, mentoring networks, incubators, accelerators, advisory groups, or related entrepreneurship initiatives. Experience building partnerships with entrepreneurs, employers, alumni, community organizations, and other external stakeholders. Previous college-level teaching experience. Experience with program assessment, curriculum development, student recruitment, or co-curricular program management. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references. All applications/resumes must be submitted through this online process. We regret that we are unable to accept applications or resumes submitted by mail, email, or fax. As you are submitting your application via this online process, please be sure to provide an accurate email address. You will then receive an acknowledgment indicating your application materials have been received. Marietta College is an equal opportunity educator and employer. Marietta College does not discriminate on the basis of age, race, color, gender orientation, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, religion, sex, pregnancy (including childbirth, lactation and related medical conditions), physical or mental disability, genetic information (including testing and characteristics), veteran status, uniformed service member status, political affiliation, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local laws. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Marietta College 215 Fifth Street, Marietta, OH 45750"
    }
  },
